API}]{assets/code/first-poc-radial-menu.vue}

Making a trame widget out of the Vue components was quite fast.

Then there was a code review phase, correcting the style, the comments, the
functions used, with Lucie.

Finally when everything was ready, the project was put on a Kitware owned
repository and published to PyPI through a GitHub workflow \cite{github-actions}.

Now when new features are asked, they are added to the issues, I make a PR which
is also reviewed by Lucie and then merged, like
\cref{pr:Kitware/trame-radial-menu/1}.
